// DRAFT (Act III, planning only). Ch19 I07 "The signatures" (C, 1.5 min). act3_ch19.md §2 I07. The crown's antechamber:
// a lectern with a duty roll. Ysolde turns it: the same two hands, signing every watch, for four hundred years.
// RULE 3: how the party knows the Abiding is the hands Ysolde saw in the Archive's ledgers (Ch13).
title: ch19_the_signatures
location: ch19/iskarra_spire
---
@letterbox on
@camera I05
@music silence fade=1.0
@mark ysolde duty_lectern walk
@anim ysolde turn_page duty_roll
@wait 3.0
@camera I06
Duty roll, the anchor-engine, Iskarra: Watch kept. H. Oan. Entered, I. Rue. #line:ch19_roll_001 #narration #tn:"One line of a duty roll, repeated for four hundred years. Shown in the document reader."
@wait 3.0
<<if $ch13_read_ledgers>>
    Ysolde [cold]: I've seen these hands. In the Archive. On every page. #line:ch19_sig_001
<<else>>
    Ysolde [cold]: The same two hands. Every watch. Four hundred years of them. #line:ch19_sig_002
<<endif>>
@wait 2.0
Kerrid [neutral]: Somebody's still on watch, then. #line:ch19_sig_003
@letterbox off
<<event start_battle ch19_abiding_wardens>>
===
